{"kind":"propose","text":"PB-3 signatures before source. In one client module I propose `watchLive(options: LiveWatchOptions): LiveWatch` and `openPresence(options: PresenceOptions): Presence`. `LiveWatchOptions` holds the room origin, full ScopeRef, definition Digest, an abort-aware session supplier and a bound transport. `LiveWatch` exposes `frames: AsyncIterable\u003cLiveSnapshot\u003e`, `close(): Promise\u003cvoid\u003e` and `done: Promise\u003cvoid\u003e`. `LiveSnapshot` holds `{scope, definition, generation, tick, rows}` with complete authorized items and exact ID/revision. `PresenceOptions` extends the watch options with declared act names `{enter, update, renew?, leave}`, `leaseMs`, `renewEveryMs`, `debounceMs`, a pure `selectOwnRow(rows)` callback and an injected abort-aware `sign({kind,on,expected,fields}, signal): Promise\u003cSignedIntent\u003e`. The caller owns signing authority. `Presence` exposes `set(fields): void`, `leave(): Promise\u003cvoid\u003e`, `close(): Promise\u003cvoid\u003e` and `done: Promise\u003cvoid\u003e`. An application observes checked snapshots and state transitions, and calls leave or close on page hide. Session replacement closes the previous watch. On reset use the new complete snapshot and re-enter. After an unknown act answer wait for checked state, and never sign a revision guessed from the answer tick.\n\nNative `/live-stream` currently emits only `{generation,tick}` and coalesces unread notices (scope/src/live-reads.ts, scope/src/sessions.ts). The applied tick proves an opened ID only, while existing rows increment their own revision in derive/src/fold.ts. Existing Map reads summaries around acts for this reason. A client alone cannot provide watched rows and remove those reads. I propose one opt-in authenticated snapshot format on the same live-stream path, selected by Accept. It would reuse the checked live summary visibility, bind full scope and definition, and send a complete bounded snapshot initially, after coalesced changes and on generation reset. Preserve existing tick-only clients; no new query or gateway route. Enforce frame size and row bounds and refuse an incomplete snapshot. Apply the existing session gate per snapshot. Measure real stream frames and bytes before deciding if bounded deltas are needed. An alternative keeps tick notices and reads after invalidations including own changes, which requires changing the PB-1 rule. Please rule on the exported signatures, the minimal room-side format and its frame bound. The B4 browser currently acts on projected offers and will stay on that path unless the shared module can preserve its exact behavior. The 45/15 schedule yields 240 renewal acts per tab-hour plus moves and enters/leaves. The native witness will measure those separately from session refresh, watch traffic, reconnects, retries and unknown answers."}